***************************** T A L Y S **************************1625 1451  187
                                                                  1625 1451  188
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1625 1451  189
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1625 1451  190
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1625 1451  191
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1625 1451  192
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1625 1451  193
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1625 1451  194
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1625 1451  195
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1625 1451  196
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1625 1451  197
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1625 1451  198
stored in this data file:                                         1625 1451  199
                                                                  1625 1451  200
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1625 1451  201
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1625 1451  202
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1625 1451  203
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1625 1451  204
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1625 1451  205
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1625 1451  206
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1625 1451  207
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1625 1451  208
- Recoil data                                                     1625 1451  209
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1625 1451  210
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1625 1451  211
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1625 1451  212
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1625 1451  213
- Residual production cross sections                              1625 1451  214
                                                                  1625 1451  215
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1625 1451  216
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1625 1451  217
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1625 1451  218
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1625 1451  219
                                                                  1625 1451  220
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************1625 1451  221
